#### Grammar 1: 만큼
**Meaning and Usage:** This is used with a noun to show the extent that something is similar to the word that comes before it. When '~ 만큼 ~은/는 없다' is used, it is used as a superlative.

**Examples:**
1. 아들이 아버지만큼 키가 컸다. - The son have grown as tall as their father.
2. 그 아이는 어른만큼 밥을 많이 먹는다. - That child eats as much as an adult.
3. 여행한 곳 중에서 제주도만큼 아름다운 곳이 없었어요. - Among all the places I've visited, there was no place as beautiful as Jeju Island.
4. 우리 반에서 유키 씨만큼 열심히 공부하는 학생은 없어요. - There is no student in our class who studies as diligently as Yuki.
5. 가: 우리 반에서 누가 요리를 제일 잘해요? / 나: 레오 씨만큼 요리를 잘하는 사람은 없어요. - A: Who cooks the best in our class? / B: There isn't anyone who cooks as well as Leo.
6. 가: 유키 씨 고향은 겨울에 날씨가 추워요? / 나: 네, 서울의 겨울만큼 추워요. - A: Yuki, is it cold in the winter in your hometown? / B: Yes, it's as cold as Seoul.

**Note:** This is not used with nouns of clear quantities in which judgment of extent is not needed. 예) 커피 한 잔만큼 주세요. (x) 냉면 한 그릇만큼 주세요. (x)

#### Grammar 2: -어도/아도/여도
**Meaning and Usage:** This is used with an action or descriptive verb to show that although the content at the beginning of the sentence is assumed or acknowledged, it has no relationship to or influence over the content that follows.

**Form:** '-아도' is used when an action or descriptive verb stem ends with 'ㅏ, ㅗ' and '-어도' is used when it ends with the other vowels 'ㅓ,ㅜ,ㅡ,ㅣ.' '-여도'(해도) is used when the verb stem ends with '하-.'

**Examples:**
1. 책을 여러 번 읽어도 모르겠어요. - I still don't understand even after reading the book many times.
2. 택시를 타고 가도 늦을 것 같아요. - I think I will be late even if I take a taxi to go there.
3. 아무리 바빠도 밥을 먹어야 해요. - No matter how busy you are, you still have to eat.
4. 유키 씨가 똑똑한 사람이어도 이 문제는 어려워할 거예요. - Even though Yuki is an intelligent person, she will still have difficulty with this problem.
5. 가: 좀 피곤한데 숙제를 안 해도 돼요? / 나: 피곤해도 숙제는 해야 돼요. - A: I'm tired so must I really do my homework? / B: Yes, you must do your homework even if you're tired.
6. 가: 내일 눈이 오면 레오 씨가 등산을 안 갈까요? / 나: 아니요, 레오 씨는 눈이 와도 등산을 갈 거예요. - A: Do you think Leo won't go hiking if it snows tomorrow? / B: No, Leo will still go hiking even if it snows.

